From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: End a source load that completes after shutdown.

The load callback returned at once when the engine had been shut down,
without calling IMFSourceResolver::End*(). The resolver keeps a
completed request until End*() is called, and the result it keeps
holds the engine's load callback and with it the engine, which holds
the resolver: closing a video while it is still loading leaked the
engine. A source created for that load was never shut down either,
and a media source is not freed before it is shut down; the
application that creates a source through the resolver has to shut
it down.

The callback now calls End*() first, with the same byte stream or URL
selection as before. After shutdown it then releases the engine lock
and shuts the source down, as media_engine_clear_presentation() does
outside the lock, and returns without creating a topology or sending
events. A failed request is just ended. Loads that complete before
shutdown behave as before.

The test registers a local byte stream handler, shuts the engine down
while the load is pending and then completes it, from a URL and from a
byte stream, with a source and with an error; the source must be shut
down and the engine must release its callback. Waits are bounded.

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
index 0be7183..61abbb2 100644
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1550,9 +1550,31 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_load_handler_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *iface,
 
     EnterCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
 
+    /* End the request also after shutdown: until then the resolver keeps this result, which holds a
+       reference to the engine. */
+    if (SUCCEEDED(IMFAsyncResult_GetState(result, &state)))
+    {
+        hr = IMFSourceResolver_EndCreateObjectFromByteStream(engine->resolver, result, &obj_type, &object);
+        IUnknown_Release(state);
+    }
+    else
+        hr = IMFSourceResolver_EndCreateObjectFromURL(engine->resolver, result, &obj_type, &object);
+
     if (engine->flags & FLAGS_ENGINE_SHUT_DOWN)
     {
         media_engine_unlock(engine);
+
+        /* Nobody else will shut the abandoned source down, and a source is not freed before that. The
+           engine lock is not held, as in media_engine_clear_presentation(). */
+        if (object)
+        {
+            if (SUCCEEDED(IUnknown_QueryInterface(object, &IID_IMFMediaSource, (void **)&source)))
+            {
+                IMFMediaSource_Shutdown(source);
+                IMFMediaSource_Release(source);
+            }
+            IUnknown_Release(object);
+        }
         return S_OK;
     }
 
@@ -1562,14 +1584,6 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_load_handler_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *iface,
     start_playback = engine->flags & FLAGS_ENGINE_PLAY_PENDING;
     media_engine_set_flag(engine, FLAGS_ENGINE_SOURCE_PENDING | FLAGS_ENGINE_PLAY_PENDING, FALSE);
 
-    if (SUCCEEDED(IMFAsyncResult_GetState(result, &state)))
-    {
-        hr = IMFSourceResolver_EndCreateObjectFromByteStream(engine->resolver, result, &obj_type, &object);
-        IUnknown_Release(state);
-    }
-    else
-        hr = IMFSourceResolver_EndCreateObjectFromURL(engine->resolver, result, &obj_type, &object);
-
     if (FAILED(hr))
         WARN("Failed to create source object, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
 
